# AREA CORE4 — auxiliary objects for Bender §4 (8) (the index bound)

Bender 1981, p. 226, derives the index bound `|U : B₀ K F(U)| ≤ p` of §4 (8) from the following
objects, which are *not* part of `Case2Data`/`Case2SevenFacts` and therefore have to be built:

* `A`: "the subgroup of type `(p,p)` in `F × K₁`" (`K₁ = K₀ = F(U) ⊓ K`).  Since `K` and `F`
  commute and meet trivially (`K ⊓ F ≤ K ⊓ B₀ = ⊥`, both normal in `U ⊓ M`) and are cyclic, this is
  exactly the p-torsion of `F ⊔ K`, i.e. `Asub D p = Ω₁(F ⊔ K)`; it has order `p²` and exponent
  `p`, and it contains every subgroup of `F ⊔ K` with these properties.  `P ≤ F` of order `p`
  lies in it.
* `Q := Ω₁(Z₂(O_p(U)))`: the subgroup generated by the elements of order dividing `p` inside the
  *second centre* of the p-core of `U` — see `Qsub`.

Everything here is stated for a general finite group `G`; `p` is the odd prime of §4 (8) (the
order of the subgroup `P ≤ F`).

The definitions are deliberately "closure"-shaped, so that the lemma layer can state the
mathematical content (`Qsub` is normal in `U`, has exponent `p`, is non-cyclic; the trichotomy of
`Asub` and `Qsub`) without any closure bookkeeping in the definitions themselves.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.CORE4.Defs

open scoped commutatorElement

namespace Work.CORE4

open Work.GW2 Subgroup

variable {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G]

/-- `{x ∈ P | x ^ p = 1}`, the set of elements of `P` of order dividing `p`. -/
def omega1Set (p : ℕ) (P : Subgroup G) : Set G := {x | x ∈ P ∧ x ^ p = 1}

/-- `Ω₁(P)`: the subgroup generated by the elements of `P` of order dividing `p`.

For a finite abelian `P` this is the p-torsion `{x ∈ P | x ^ p = 1}`; the closure formulation
avoids proving that up front. -/
noncomputable def omega1 (p : ℕ) (P : Subgroup G) : Subgroup G :=
  Subgroup.closure (omega1Set p P)

/-- The second centre of `P`, as a set: `{x ∈ P | [x, P] ≤ Z(P)}`.  (Written with the triple
commutator so that it can be used without coercing into `↥P`.) -/
def z2Set (P : Subgroup G) : Set G :=
  {x | x ∈ P ∧ ∀ y ∈ P, ∀ z ∈ P, ⁅⁅x, y⁆, z⁆ = 1}

/-- `Z₂(P)`: the subgroup generated by the second centre of `P`. -/
noncomputable def z2 (P : Subgroup G) : Subgroup G := Subgroup.closure (z2Set P)

/-- `Z(P)` (the centre of `P`) viewed as a subgroup of `G`, for a subgroup `P ≤ G`. -/
noncomputable def centerIn (P : Subgroup G) : Subgroup G :=
  (Subgroup.center ↥P).map P.subtype

/-- Bender's `Q := Ω₁(Z₂(O_p(U)))` (p. 226), where `O_p(U) = pCoreIn p B.U`. -/
noncomputable def Qsub (p : ℕ) (B : BenderSetup G) : Subgroup G :=
  omega1 p (z2 (pCoreIn p B.U))
/-- Bender's `A`, "the subgroup of type `(p,p)` in `F × K₁`": the p-torsion of `F ⊔ K`, i.e.
`Ω₁(F ⊔ K)`.  (`K₁ = K ⊓ F(U)`, and `K ⊓ F(U)` contains the unique subgroup of order `p` of the
cyclic `K` as soon as `p ∣ |K|`, so this is the same as `Ω₁(F ⊔ K₁)`.) -/
noncomputable def Asub {B : BenderSetup G} (D : Case2Data B) (p : ℕ) : Subgroup G :=
  omega1 p (D.F ⊔ D.K)

end Work.CORE4
